2025-10-08 12:27:11,787 [WARNING] Skipped idx=560: gold or llm supporting sentence is empty. gold='', llm='The p73 gene encodes two main isoforms: TAp73 and DeltaNp73. TAp73 is the transcriptionally active form, while DeltaNp73 is a dominant-negative acting form. These isoforms are differentially expressed in various tissues, including the brain and glial tumors. In normal brain tissues, the expression of p73 is low or undetectable. In glial tumors, particularly in high-grade gliomas, there is a strong up-regulation of TAp73, which may reflect the inactivation of the retinoblastoma pathway leading to the activation of E2F transcription factors, as TAp73 is a known target of E2F1 gene. The study of TAp73 expression in brain tumors can provide insights into the retinoblastoma pathway-dependent tumor progression.'
